WEBVTT

00:00:01.50 --> 00:00:06.34
This is journey thirty five of Hewn, the software factory: choose a theme.

00:00:06.34 --> 00:00:09.87
Anyone who signs in to Mission Control can pick Light,

00:00:09.87 --> 00:00:11.96
Dark or System for their device.

00:00:11.96 --> 00:00:16.02
This video shows the choice being made and surviving a reload,

00:00:16.02 --> 00:00:20.46
the operating system changing the theme live, how the tokens switch,

00:00:20.46 --> 00:00:23.60
and the tests that hold contrast in both themes.

00:00:24.75 --> 00:00:26.71
The requirement has two parts.

00:00:26.71 --> 00:00:32.14
With no saved choice, Mission Control follows the operating system's colour scheme.

00:00:32.14 --> 00:00:37.63
And when the user picks Light, Dark or System, their choice is kept across a reload,

00:00:37.63 --> 00:00:42.14
with text contrast of at least four and a half to one in both themes.

00:00:43.29 --> 00:00:44.39
Here is Settings.

00:00:44.39 --> 00:00:48.46
The new Appearance section sits at the top, with System chosen,

00:00:48.46 --> 00:00:50.72
because nothing has been saved yet.

00:00:50.72 --> 00:00:54.27
The Owner picks Dark, and the whole page turns at once.

00:00:54.27 --> 00:00:57.83
They reload, and it stays dark, with Dark still chosen.

00:00:57.83 --> 00:01:00.87
Then Light, and another reload: light it stays.

00:01:00.87 --> 00:01:05.39
Finally System, which hands the decision back to the operating system.

00:01:06.54 --> 00:01:11.48
With System chosen, the operating system's setting is followed live.

00:01:11.48 --> 00:01:14.96
The clip switches the OS between light and dark,

00:01:14.96 --> 00:01:18.88
and Mission Control follows each time, with no reload.

00:01:18.88 --> 00:01:22.22
A saved Light or Dark ignores the OS entirely.

00:01:23.37 --> 00:01:26.99
The choice is per device, and a Viewer can make it too.

00:01:26.99 --> 00:01:32.32
On a phone, the menu drawer, Projects and the project page all draw in the chosen

00:01:32.32 --> 00:01:32.71
theme.

00:01:33.86 --> 00:01:36.70
The design tokens already held both themes.

00:01:36.70 --> 00:01:41.06
Every colour is a role, like the default foreground or the canvas,

00:01:41.06 --> 00:01:46.21
and the dark values are set in two places: on a root with the dark data theme,

00:01:46.21 --> 00:01:51.03
and under the dark colour scheme media query, unless the root says light.

00:01:51.03 --> 00:01:53.67
So the app never had to change a colour.

00:01:53.67 --> 00:01:56.18
It only sets or removes one attribute.

00:01:56.53 --> 00:02:02.33
The theme service reads the saved choice from local storage under hewn dot theme.

00:02:02.33 --> 00:02:06.91
Light and Dark set the data theme attribute on the html element.

00:02:06.91 --> 00:02:10.21
System removes it, so the media query decides.

00:02:10.21 --> 00:02:13.57
If storage can't be read, the choice is System.

00:02:13.92 --> 00:02:19.83
A short script in index html applies a saved Light or Dark before the first paint,

00:02:19.83 --> 00:02:22.86
so a reload never flashes the other theme.

00:02:22.86 --> 00:02:27.62
Settings' radios read the service's choice signal and call choose.

00:02:27.97 --> 00:02:31.36
The class diagram shows Settings driving the service,

00:02:31.36 --> 00:02:34.04
which works through three small functions.

00:02:34.04 --> 00:02:36.72
The sequence shows the choice being saved,

00:02:36.72 --> 00:02:39.85
and the reload applying it before Angular starts.

00:02:41.00 --> 00:02:46.80
The theme functions have four unit tests: no choice or an unknown one is System,

00:02:46.80 --> 00:02:51.58
a saved Light or Dark reads back, a save survives blocked storage,

00:02:51.58 --> 00:02:53.97
and System removes the attribute.

00:02:53.97 --> 00:02:57.66
They failed first, because the module didn't exist.

00:02:58.01 --> 00:03:02.93
The behaviour tests run in the browser with the OS preference emulated.

00:03:02.93 --> 00:03:06.68
With no choice, the page follows the OS as it changes.

00:03:06.68 --> 00:03:10.28
Dark and Light override the OS and survive a reload.

00:03:10.28 --> 00:03:12.57
System goes back to following it.

00:03:12.57 --> 00:03:15.48
And a Viewer's choice shows on every page.

00:03:15.48 --> 00:03:19.77
They failed first, because Settings had no Appearance section.

00:03:20.12 --> 00:03:24.32
The contrast scan runs axe core on every page in light and in dark,

00:03:24.32 --> 00:03:26.63
and on a saved choice against the OS.

00:03:26.63 --> 00:03:29.89
It found something on the way: right after a switch,

00:03:29.89 --> 00:03:33.77
links ease their colour for a hundred and twenty milliseconds,

00:03:33.77 --> 00:03:35.58
and axe caught them mid fade.

00:03:35.58 --> 00:03:38.34
The scan now waits for the switch to finish.

00:03:38.34 --> 00:03:43.59
To prove it would catch a real problem, a dark text token was dropped to near black:

00:03:43.59 --> 00:03:44.72
every page failed.

00:03:44.72 --> 00:03:46.60
With the real tokens, none do.

00:03:46.95 --> 00:03:51.28
The visual tests compare Appearance with its mock, in light and in dark.

00:03:52.43 --> 00:03:54.65
Journey thirty five is complete.

00:03:54.65 --> 00:03:59.73
Mission Control follows the operating system until you choose, and Light,

00:03:59.73 --> 00:04:03.41
Dark or System is kept on your device across reloads,

00:04:03.41 --> 00:04:05.56
applied before the first paint.

00:04:05.56 --> 00:04:11.40
Both themes hold four and a half to one contrast on every page, checked by axe core.

00:04:11.40 --> 00:04:13.48
Next comes journey thirty six.
